    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Viersche',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Viersche (Hundert/Hunderte) is a Black Forest German partnership trick-taking game. 4 players in 2 teams. 36-card deck. 9 cards each. Bottom card = trump. Forehand MUST lead trump first trick (if no trumps, lead face-down). Race to 100+ card points. First to claim 100 wins; erase 4 'rungs' to win session.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Viersche (also Hundert or Hunderte) is a point-trick game local to the Wolf and Kinzig valleys in the Black Forest of Germany. It was first recorded on a 1932 map of the most common card games in Baden, republished in Friedrich Schlager's 1951 article on Cego; the centre of play was the Wolf valley, with other clusters near Oberharmersbach, Baiersbronn, St. Georgen, Villingen and Geisingen. It is the forward version of Hindersche (Swabian: viersche = forwards, hindersche = backwards), which was played by foresters, farmers and journeymen in the old Principality of Fürstenberg; anticlockwise play and the ranking of the ten suggest the game may be two or three centuries old. It is likely a descendant of Réunion, a German game once popular in the Rhineland and along the Neckar. Since at least 2003, annual tournaments have been held around Epiphany in Bad Rippoldsau.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 (2 fixed teams)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36 cards. A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6. Bottom card = trump.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, slate/chalk for scoring',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '9 each in packets of 3. Bottom card turned up = trump.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
